  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1240 AM MDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nUpper ridge amplifies slightly Thu/Fri as center of upper high\ndrifts westward toward AZ, then flow flattens over the weekend\ninto early next week as upper trough digs into the Pacific NW \nand upper jet sags south through the Rockies. Still plenty of\nmoisture around on Thu with CAPE approaching 1000 J/KG in spots,\nand with NW flow aloft carrying storms away from the mountains\ninto the I-25 corridor, expect another rather active thunderstorm\nday, though eastward extent of storms may be limited by slightly\nweaker instability over the far east. Can't rule out heavy rain\nonce again, especially over the ern mountains and along I-25. \nFri/Sat look drier as lee surface trough deepens on the plains \nand low level flow takes on a more wly downslope look both days.  \nStill can't rule out a storm anywhere in the CWA, though \nactivity looks more isolated and weaker than earlier in the \nweek. Temps Thu will again run near/slightly cooler than \naverage, then some slight warming expected Fri/Sat with heights \nbeginning to rise and downslope mixing developing. Upper jet \nthen sags far enough south to enhance thunderstorm chance from \nSun into early next week, as mid level moisture flows back into \nthe area and low levels potentially moisten as well behind a \nlate weekend/early week cold front.",
